1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,360
of the towers collapsed onto the lower one.

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:06,040
The upper and lower sections should have mutually destroyed each other until all the

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:09,400
energy is dissipated and the system comes to arrest.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,120
What could not have happened is this.

5
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:17,320
A little tiny chunk of the building can't possibly fall and crush the entire structure

6
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,320
below it.

7
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:22,320
This is such a simple fundamental concept that architects and engineers were astonished

8
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:24,720
in seeing it totally ignored by NIST.

9
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:30,680
This is high school physics and our whole society is being led to believe that these

10
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:35,840
fundamental laws of physics, hard science, don't apply anymore.

11
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,640
But even if we assumed that the top section of the tower had enough potential energy

12
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:44,000
to destroy the rest of the structure below, it could not have done so at the speed it

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
did, which was near free fall speed.

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,240
That would have violated an even more important principle in physics, known as the law of

15
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:53,680
momentum conservation.

16
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:58,640
This law states that the total energy within an isolated system must always remain the

17
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:59,640
same.

18
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:04,400
As we have seen, the energy can be transformed within the system, from motion to physical

19
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,920
deformation.

20
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:11,360
But for the deformation to begin, the velocity must decrease in order for one kind of energy

21
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:14,040
to be transformed into the other.

22
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:17,200
No new energy can be added to the system.

23
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,120
One particular example of momentum conservation is free fall.

24
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:25,360
Free fall happens when the only force applied on an object is gravity.

25
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:30,200
This means that all the potential energy contained by the object is converted into vertical

26
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,280
motion.

27
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:35,960
As soon as the falling object hits an obstacle and breakage occurs, the speed must decrease

28
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:40,560
because some of its energy needs now to be converted into physical breakage.

29
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:45,320
It takes energy to break things apart and that energy must come from within the system.

30
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:49,720
Thus, the falling rock cannot keep falling at free fall speed and break apart at the

31
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:54,480
same time because it doesn't have enough energy to do both.

32
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:58,080
Let's go now to the twin towers and ask a simple question.

33
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:01,760
Assuming that the top section on the left contains enough potential energy to destroy

34
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:06,200
the rest of the tower and assuming we dropped both upper sections at the same time, which

35
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,400
one would hit the ground first.

36
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,440
It would be the second, of course.

37
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:14,640
As it finds no obstacles in its path, the section on the right would quickly accelerate

38
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:18,920
the free fall speed and maintain it all the way to the ground.

39
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:23,240
The section on the left instead needs to use some of its energy to destroy the structure

40
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:27,140
below so it could never achieve free fall speed.

41
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:31,480
In the case of the twin towers, however, both upper sections fell with an acceleration

42
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:37,760
close to free fall speed as if their path had been practically free from obstacles.

43
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:42,400
It took each tower between 10 and 12 seconds to collapse to the ground while an absolute

44
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,240
free fall time would have been 9.2 seconds.

